      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions: <Subject 1> is the original main person in <Video 1>, whose role is being replaced. Only their body position, pose, movement, gestures, expressions, timing and clothing fit from the reel are used as performance. <Subject 2> is the target adult AI persona shown in both <Picture 1> and <Picture 2>; facial identity, hair, skin tone and body identity come only from those photographs. <Picture 1> is a frontal/clear face photograph of <Subject 2>. <Picture 2> is a complementary three-quarter face and upper-body view of the same <Subject 2>. Neither picture depicts the original performer. <Video 1> is the source reel: shot order, composition, camera, environment, clothing, props, poses, expressions, action and timing. <Audio 1> is the connected soundtrack of <Video 1>, used as a model reference and exported as the final audio.\n\nretention_analysis: <Video 1> (camera framing, camera motion, environment, background, lighting, clothing, choreography and timing): fully_preserved. <Subject 1>: partially_preserved - body position, pose, movement path, gestures, expressions and timing are kept; facial identity is replaced by <Subject 2>. <Subject 2>: attribute_transfer - face, hair and body identity from <Picture 1> and <Picture 2> replace <Subject 1>, mapped onto the same pose and movement at every moment, wearing the clothing from <Video 1>. <Audio 1>: fully_copy.\n\nrecreation_rules: The target video is a photorealistic recreation of <Video 1> with <Subject 2> performing <Subject 1>'s role. Preserve cuts, framing and timing from the reel. Photographs are identity references, not first/last frames. Do not redesign the scene or invent a new camera path.\n\naudio_roles: Export and condition on the original <Audio 1> soundtrack. Preserve its words, voices, pauses, laughter, ambience and music. Do not request a new persona voice."
      ],
      "title": "01 - Fixed roles (Subject 1 original / Subject 2 persona)",
      "color": "#232",
      "bgcolor": "#353"
